# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example crontab for tarxiv database backups.
#
# Install with:  crontab -e   (paste below)   or   crontab scripts/backup.crontab.example
# Inspect with:  crontab -l
#
# This runs ON the server that hosts the Docker stack, so the scripts talk to
# a LOCAL Docker engine / Couchbase — no SSH or remote hosts involved. Each
# script handles its own retention, so cron just fires them.
#
# To keep an off-site copy, run a separate rsync job on your OTHER box that
# pulls the backup dirs from here (see the note at the bottom).
#
# Cron runs with a bare environment (no login shell), so we set PATH and the
# paths explicitly here. Adjust them to your server.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
# Email any stderr/cron output here (needs a working MTA); leave blank to disable.
MAILTO=""

# Absolute path to your checkout of the repo on the server.
TARXIV_REPO=/opt/tarxiv

# Where the dumps are written. Defaults live under the repo's .data dir, but a
# dedicated location is easier for the rsync job on the other box to target.
TARXIV_BACKUP_DIR=/srv/backups/tarxiv/postgres
# Portable JSONL dumps from db_utils.py --backup.
TARXIV_COUCHBASE_BACKUP_DIR=/srv/backups/tarxiv/couchbase/jsonl
# The cbbackupmgr archive dir is TARXIV_COUCHBASE_ARCHIVE_DIR in setup/.env
# (e.g. /srv/backups/tarxiv/couchbase/cbbackupmgr); it must not be the JSONL dir.

# Optional: override the GFS retention windows (defaults shown).
# TARXIV_KEEP_DAILY_DAYS=7
# TARXIV_KEEP_WEEKLY_DAYS=90
# TARXIV_KEEP_MONTHLY_DAYS=365
# cbbackupmgr keeps TARXIV_COUCHBASE_KEEP_MONTHS monthly repos (setup/.env, default 12).

#   min  hour  dom  mon  dow   command
# Postgres dump every day at 02:30.
30   2    *    *    *    cd $TARXIV_REPO && ./scripts/backup_postgres.sh >> /var/log/tarxiv/pg-backup.log 2>&1

# Couchbase cbbackupmgr backup (every scope; incremental within a month) at 03:00.
0    3    *    *    *    cd $TARXIV_REPO && ./scripts/backup_couchbase.sh >> /var/log/tarxiv/couchbase-backup.log 2>&1

# Optional: weekly portable JSONL dump (every scope), Sundays at 04:00.
0    4    *    *    0    cd $TARXIV_REPO && uv run --env-file setup/.env python scripts/db_utils.py --backup >> /var/log/tarxiv/couchbase-jsonl-backup.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# * mkdir -p /var/log/tarxiv  (and chown it to the cron user) first, or the
#   redirects above will fail silently.
# * `uv` must be on PATH for the cron user. If it lives in ~/.local/bin or
#   ~/.cargo/bin, add that dir to PATH above, or call it by absolute path.
# * The postgres and couchbase scripts load setup/.env for credentials and use
#   the local compose `postgres` / `couchbase-backup` services. Values in
#   setup/.env win over the ones set here. db_utils.py connects via TarxivDB
#   using the usual local Couchbase config (TARXIV_COUCHBASE_HOST etc.), so make
#   sure that resolves for the cron user — typically localhost on the host.
# * The cbbackupmgr container writes the archive as root, so run
#   backup_couchbase.sh as root or make sure the rsync user can read it.
# * The cbbackupmgr archive is a single unit: rsync the whole directory, never
#   cherry-pick files out of it.
# * Off-site copy: on your other box, a pull-based rsync keeps a remote copy,
#   e.g. a cron line there like:
#       15 5 * * * rsync -az --delete \
#         server.internal:/srv/backups/tarxiv/ /srv/backups/tarxiv-mirror/
#   Schedule it after these jobs finish (here 05:15, after the Sunday 04:00 dump).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
